/-!
# Axiomatizable formations of groups that are not varieties (Kourovka Notebook Problem 14.32)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.32 (A. M. Gaglione, D. Spellman): define a
formation of (not necessarily finite) groups as a nonempty class closed under homomorphic images and
subdirect products with finitely many factors. Must every first-order axiomatizable formation of
groups be a variety? The main result, `axiomatizableFormationIsVariety_refuted`, shows that the
answer is no: some class of groups is a formation and is first-order axiomatizable but is not a
variety.

## The counterexample

Kearnes proved more (see the source below); this file exhibits a single counterexample, built
from the alternating group `S = A₅`, a finite simple group with trivial centre. Call a group `G`
*locally an image of powers of `S`* when every finite subset of `G` lies in the image of a
homomorphism `Sⁿ → G` from some finite direct power of `S`.

* The class is closed under surjective homomorphic images.
* It is first-order axiomatizable: for each `k`, a sentence says that every `k` elements lie in the
  image of a homomorphism from `S^(Sᵏ)`, written with one variable for each element of `S^(Sᵏ)`
  and its multiplication table. Any `k` elements of an image of `Sⁿ` lie in an image of `S^(Sᵏ)`:
  choose preimages and group the coordinates of `Sⁿ` by the values the preimages take there.
* It contains `S` but not the cyclic subgroup generated by a nontrivial element of `S`, since every
  homomorphism from a power of `S` to a group smaller than `S` is trivial. A variety is closed
  under subgroups, so the class is not a variety.

The substance is closure under subdirect products of two factors. Let `R ≤ A × B` have surjective
projections, with `A` and `B` in the class, and let `X ⊆ R` be finite. Choose images `f(Sᵖ) ⊆ A`
and `g(S^q) ⊆ B` containing the coordinates of `X`, lifts to `R` of their elements, and images of
powers of `S` containing all coordinates of these finitely many elements. They combine into a
homomorphism `F` from a power `Sᵐ` to `A × B`; let `H = F⁻¹(R)` and let `D ≤ H` be the subgroup
generated by the images of homomorphisms `S → H`. Three facts about `S` are used:

* an image of `S` in a quotient of a subgroup of `Sᵐ` lifts to an image of `S` in that subgroup,
  because a subgroup of minimal order mapping onto the image is itself a copy of `S`;
* a subgroup of `Sᵐ` whose coordinate projections are each trivial or all of `S` is the image of
  a power of `S` (induction on `m`); in particular `D` is;
* no quotient of a power of `S` has a nontrivial centre.

By the first fact, the projections of `Q = F(D)` contain `f(Sᵖ)` and `g(S^q)`; and `F(H)`
normalizes `Q`. For `x ∈ X`, pick `q ∈ Q` with the first coordinate of `x`; then `q⁻¹x = (1, n)`
normalizes `Q`, so `n` is central modulo `{m | (1, m) ∈ Q}` in the second projection of `Q`, and
the third fact gives `(1, n) ∈ Q`. Hence `X ⊆ Q`, which is an image of a power of `S`.

## Main declarations

* `IsFormation`, `IsAxiomatizable`, `IsVariety`: formations in the sense of Gaglione and
  Spellman, first-order axiomatizable classes and varieties of groups.
* `axiomatizableFormationIsVariety`: the Gaglione–Spellman question.
* `axiomatizableFormationIsVariety_refuted`: its negative answer.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AxiomatizableFormationVarietyKourovka14Problem32Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.32 (A. M.
Gaglione, D. Spellman). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701017 (`KOU-14.32`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath
v1.8.0.

Classes of groups are predicates on groups in `Type`. Subdirect products of finitely many factors
are expressed by `G / N₁, G / N₂ ∈ 𝔉 → G / (N₁ ∩ N₂) ∈ 𝔉`, which together with homomorphic images
gives all of them. Axiomatizable means "the groups in the class are the models of a first-order
theory in the language of groups" (`MathlibExt`'s `groupLanguage`); a variety is the class of groups
satisfying a set of laws.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language

/-- A class of groups, as a predicate on groups in `Type`. -/
abbrev GroupClass : Type 1 := ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], Prop

/-- **Formations of groups in the sense of Gaglione and Spellman.** A class $\mathfrak{F}$ of
groups is a formation when it contains at least one group, it is closed under surjective
homomorphic images (if $G \in \mathfrak{F}$ and $\varphi \colon G \to H$ is a surjective
homomorphism, then $H \in \mathfrak{F}$), and for every group $G$ and all normal subgroups $N_1$,
$N_2$ of $G$, if $G/N_1$ and $G/N_2$ lie in $\mathfrak{F}$, then so does $G/(N_1 \cap N_2)$.

Together with closure under homomorphic images, the last condition amounts to closure under
subdirect products of finitely many factors; the groups need not be finite. -/
def IsFormation (𝔉 : GroupClass) : Prop :=
  (∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), 𝔉 G) ∧
    (∀ (G H : Type) [Group G] [Group H] (φ : G →* H), Function.Surjective φ → 𝔉 G → 𝔉 H) ∧
    ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] (N₁ N₂ : Subgroup G) [N₁.Normal] [N₂.Normal],
      𝔉 (G ⧸ N₁) → 𝔉 (G ⧸ N₂) → 𝔉 (G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂))

/-- **First-order axiomatizable classes of groups.** A class $\mathfrak{F}$ of groups is
first-order axiomatizable when there is a theory $T$ in the first-order language of groups such
that a group $G$ lies in $\mathfrak{F}$ if and only if $G$, with its canonical structure, is a
model of $T$. -/
def IsAxiomatizable (𝔉 : GroupClass) : Prop :=
  ∃ T : groupLanguage.Theory, ∀ (G : Type) [Group G],
    𝔉 G ↔ @Theory.Model groupLanguage G (groupLanguageStructure G) T

/-- **Varieties of groups.** A class $\mathfrak{F}$ of groups is a variety when there is a set
$W$ of elements of the free group on generators $x_0, x_1, x_2, \dots$ such that a group $G$ lies
in $\mathfrak{F}$ if and only if every $w \in W$ evaluates to $1$ in $G$ under every assignment of
elements of $G$ to the generators. -/
def IsVariety (𝔉 : GroupClass) : Prop :=
  ∃ W : Set (FreeGroup ℕ), ∀ (G : Type) [Group G],
    𝔉 G ↔ ∀ w ∈ W, ∀ x : ℕ → G, FreeGroup.lift x w = 1

/-- **The Gaglione–Spellman question on axiomatizable formations (Kourovka 14.32).** The
proposition that every first-order axiomatizable formation of groups is a variety: every class
$\mathfrak{F}$ of groups that is a formation and is first-order axiomatizable is a variety. -/
def axiomatizableFormationIsVariety : Prop :=
  ∀ 𝔉 : GroupClass, IsFormation 𝔉 → IsAxiomatizable 𝔉 → IsVariety 𝔉

/-! ### Homomorphisms out of a finite simple group -/

/-- A homomorphism out of a simple group is trivial or injective. -/
private theorem eq_one_or_injective {S G : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S] [Group G]
    (c : S →* G) : c = 1 ∨ Function.Injective c := by
  rcases IsSimpleGroup.eq_bot_or_eq_top_of_normal c.ker with h | h
  · exact Or.inr ((MonoidHom.ker_eq_bot_iff c).mp h)
  · exact Or.inl (MonoidHom.ker_eq_top_iff.mp h)

/-- No quotient of a power of a simple group `S` with trivial centre has a nontrivial centre: if
all commutators `[z, w]` lie in a normal subgroup `N` of `S^ι`, then so does `z`. -/
private theorem mem_of_forall_commutator_mem {S : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S]
    (hS : Subgroup.center S = ⊥) {ι : Type} [Finite ι]
    (N : Subgroup (ι → S)) [N.Normal] (z : ι → S) (hz : ∀ w, z * w * z⁻¹ * w⁻¹ ∈ N) :
    z ∈ N := by
  classical
  refine Subgroup.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem z fun i => ?_
  have hT : (N.comap (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) i)).Normal := Subgroup.Normal.comap ‹_› _
  rcases IsSimpleGroup.eq_bot_or_eq_top_of_normal (N.comap (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) i))
    with h | h
  · have hzi : z i ∈ Subgroup.center S := by
      rw [Subgroup.mem_center_iff]
      intro s
      have hmem : z i * s * (z i)⁻¹ * s⁻¹ ∈ N.comap (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) i) := by
        rw [Subgroup.mem_comap]
        convert hz (Pi.mulSingle i s) using 1
        ext j
        by_cases hj : j = i
        · subst hj; simp
        · simp [Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne hj]
      rw [h, Subgroup.mem_bot] at hmem
      have := mul_inv_eq_one.mp hmem
      rw [mul_inv_eq_iff_eq_mul] at this
      exact this.symm
    rw [hS, Subgroup.mem_bot] at hzi
    rw [hzi, Pi.mulSingle_one]
    exact N.one_mem
  · have : z i ∈ N.comap (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) i) := h ▸ Subgroup.mem_top _
    exact this

/-- The same statement for the image of a homomorphism `ρ` from a power of `S`: if `M` is
normalized by the image of `ρ` and `n` lies in that image and commutes with it modulo `M`, then
`n ∈ M`. -/
private theorem mem_of_forall_commutator_mem_range {S : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S]
    (hS : Subgroup.center S = ⊥) {B : Type} [Group B] {r : ℕ} (ρ : (Fin r → S) →* B)
    (M : Subgroup B) (hM : ∀ m ∈ M, ∀ t, ρ t * m * (ρ t)⁻¹ ∈ M) {n : B} (hn : n ∈ ρ.range)
    (hcomm : ∀ t, n * ρ t * n⁻¹ * (ρ t)⁻¹ ∈ M) : n ∈ M := by
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hn
  have hN : (M.comap ρ).Normal := ⟨fun x hx w => by
    simpa [Subgroup.mem_comap] using hM _ hx w⟩
  exact mem_of_forall_commutator_mem hS (M.comap ρ) z fun w => by
    simpa [Subgroup.mem_comap] using hcomm w

/-- **Lifting images of `S`.** Let `ψ` be a homomorphism from a finite power of a finite simple
group `S`, and `H` a subgroup of that power. Every image of `S` inside `ψ(H)` is the image under
`ψ` of an image of `S` inside `H`. A subgroup `E₀ ≤ H` of minimal order with `ψ(E₀) = c(S)` is a
copy of `S`: for each coordinate `i`, the kernel `E₁` of the `i`-th projection on `E₀` either still
maps onto `c(S)`, so `E₁ = E₀`, or lies in the kernel of `ψ`, and counting orders then shows that
the kernel of `ψ` on `E₀` is `E₁`; either way that kernel is trivial in coordinate `i`. -/
private theorem exists_lift {S : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S] [Finite S] {ι : Type}
    [Finite ι] {A : Type} [Group A] (ψ : (ι → S) →* A) (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) (c : S →* A)
    (hc : c.range ≤ H.map ψ) : ∃ c' : S →* (ι → S), c'.range ≤ H ∧ ψ.comp c' = c := by
  classical
  rcases eq_one_or_injective c with rfl | hinj
  · exact ⟨1, by simp, by simp⟩
  let P : Subgroup (ι → S) → Prop := fun E => E ≤ H ∧ E.map ψ = c.range
  have hP : P (H ⊓ c.range.comap ψ) := by
    refine ⟨inf_le_left, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
    · rw [Subgroup.map_le_iff_le_comap]; exact inf_le_right
    · intro a ha
      obtain ⟨h, hh, rfl⟩ := hc ha
      exact ⟨h, ⟨hh, ha⟩, rfl⟩
  have hex : ∃ n, ∃ E, P E ∧ Nat.card E = n := ⟨_, _, hP, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨E₀, hE₀, hcard⟩ := Nat.find_spec hex
  have hmin : ∀ E, P E → Nat.card E₀ ≤ Nat.card E := fun E hE =>
    hcard ▸ Nat.find_min' hex ⟨E, hE, rfl⟩
  let ψ₀ : E₀ →* A := ψ.comp E₀.subtype
  have hψ₀range : ψ₀.range = c.range := by
    rw [MonoidHom.range_comp, Subgroup.range_subtype]; exact hE₀.2
  have hcardS : Nat.card ψ₀.range = Nat.card S := by
    rw [hψ₀range]; exact (Nat.card_congr (MonoidHom.ofInjective hinj).toEquiv).symm
  have hker : ∀ k : E₀, ψ₀ k = 1 → k = 1 := by
    intro k hk
    apply Subtype.ext
    funext i
    let ev : E₀ →* S := (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i).comp E₀.subtype
    let E₁ : Subgroup (ι → S) := E₀ ⊓ (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i).ker
    let T : Subgroup S := (E₁.map ψ).comap c
    have hT : T.Normal := by
      refine ⟨fun t ht s => ?_⟩
      obtain ⟨e₁, he₁, he₁t⟩ := ht
      obtain ⟨e₀, he₀, he₀s⟩ : c s ∈ E₀.map ψ := hE₀.2 ▸ ⟨s, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨e₀ * e₁ * e₀⁻¹, ⟨E₀.mul_mem (E₀.mul_mem he₀ he₁.1) (E₀.inv_mem he₀), ?_⟩, ?_⟩
      · have : e₁ i = 1 := he₁.2
        simp [this]
      · simp [he₀s, he₁t]
    rcases IsSimpleGroup.eq_bot_or_eq_top_of_normal T with h | h
    · -- `E₁` lies in the kernel of `ψ`; compare orders
      have hE₁ker : ∀ e ∈ E₁, ψ e = 1 := by
        intro e he
        obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : ψ e ∈ c.range := hE₀.2 ▸ ⟨e, he.1, rfl⟩
        have htT : t ∈ T := ⟨e, he, ht.symm⟩
        rw [h, Subgroup.mem_bot] at htT
        rw [← ht, htT, map_one]
      have hle : ev.ker ≤ ψ₀.ker := fun x hx => hE₁ker x ⟨x.2, hx⟩
      have h1 := Subgroup.card_ker_mul_card_range ψ₀
      have h2 := Subgroup.card_ker_mul_card_range ev
      have h3 : Nat.card ev.range ≤ Nat.card S := Subgroup.card_le_card_group _
      have h4 : Nat.card ψ₀.ker ≤ Nat.card ev.ker := by
        rw [hcardS] at h1
        have : Nat.card ψ₀.ker * Nat.card S ≤ Nat.card ev.ker * Nat.card S := by
          rw [h1, ← h2]; exact Nat.mul_le_mul_left _ h3
        exact Nat.le_of_mul_le_mul_right this Nat.card_pos
      have heq : ev.ker = ψ₀.ker := Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge hle h4
      have : k ∈ ev.ker := heq ▸ hk
      exact this
    · -- `E₁` still maps onto `c(S)`, so `E₁ = E₀` by minimality
      have hPE₁ : P E₁ := by
        refine ⟨le_trans inf_le_left hE₀.1, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
        · rw [← hE₀.2]; exact Subgroup.map_mono inf_le_left
        · rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
          have : s ∈ T := h ▸ Subgroup.mem_top s
          exact this
      have hE : E₁ = E₀ := Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge inf_le_left (hmin E₁ hPE₁)
      have hk' : (k : ι → S) ∈ E₁ := by rw [hE]; exact k.2
      exact hk'.2
  have hinj₀ : Function.Injective ψ₀ := (injective_iff_map_eq_one ψ₀).mpr hker
  let e : E₀ ≃* ψ₀.range := MonoidHom.ofInjective hinj₀
  let c₁ : S →* ψ₀.range := c.codRestrict ψ₀.range (fun s => hψ₀range ▸ ⟨s, rfl⟩)
  refine ⟨E₀.subtype.comp (e.symm.toMonoidHom.comp c₁), ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
    exact hE₀.1 (e.symm (c₁ s)).2
  · ext s
    exact MonoidHom.apply_ofInjective_symm hinj₀ (c₁ s)

/-! ### Subgroups of powers of `S` whose projections are trivial or onto -/

section Powers

variable {S : Type} [Group S]

/-- Forgetting the first coordinate. -/
private def tailHom (m : ℕ) : (Fin (m + 1) → S) →* (Fin m → S) where
  toFun w := Fin.tail w
  map_one' := rfl
  map_mul' _ _ := rfl

/-- Inserting `1` as the first coordinate. -/
private def consOneHom (m : ℕ) : (Fin m → S) →* (Fin (m + 1) → S) where
  toFun u := Fin.cons 1 u
  map_one' := by ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun _ => ?_) j <;> simp
  map_mul' u v := by ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun _ => ?_) j <;> simp

@[simp] private theorem tailHom_apply {m : ℕ} (w : Fin (m + 1) → S) (j : Fin m) :
    tailHom m w j = w j.succ := rfl

@[simp] private theorem consOneHom_apply {m : ℕ} (u : Fin m → S) :
    consOneHom m u = Fin.cons 1 u := rfl

/-- The homomorphism `S^(r+1) → S^(m+1)` acting as the identity on the first coordinate and as
`ρ` on the others. -/
private def consHom {r m : ℕ} (ρ : (Fin r → S) →* (Fin m → S)) :
    (Fin (r + 1) → S) →* (Fin (m + 1) → S) where
  toFun t := Fin.cons (t 0) (ρ (Fin.tail t))
  map_one' := by
    ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun _ => ?_) j
    · simp
    · simp [show (Fin.tail (1 : Fin (r + 1) → S)) = 1 from rfl]
  map_mul' u v := by
    ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun _ => ?_) j
    · simp
    · simp only [Fin.cons_succ, Pi.mul_apply]
      rw [show Fin.tail (u * v) = Fin.tail u * Fin.tail v from rfl, map_mul, Pi.mul_apply]

@[simp] private theorem consHom_apply {r m : ℕ} (ρ : (Fin r → S) →* (Fin m → S))
    (t : Fin (r + 1) → S) : consHom ρ t = Fin.cons (t 0) (ρ (Fin.tail t)) := rfl

/-- Precomposition with a map of index types, as a homomorphism of powers of `S`. -/
private def precomp {α β : Type} (e : β → α) : (α → S) →* (β → S) where
  toFun w := w ∘ e
  map_one' := rfl
  map_mul' _ _ := rfl

@[simp] private theorem precomp_apply {α β : Type} (e : β → α) (w : α → S) (b : β) :
    precomp e w b = w (e b) := rfl

/-- **Subdirect powers of a simple group are images of powers.** A subgroup `D` of `Sᵐ`, for a
simple group `S`, whose coordinate projections are each trivial or all of `S`, is the image of a
homomorphism from some power of `S`. By induction on `m`: if the first projection is trivial,
`D` is a copy of its projection to the remaining coordinates; otherwise the elements of `D`
supported on the first coordinate form a normal subgroup of `S`, and `D` is either a copy of its
projection (if that subgroup is trivial) or that projection times `S`. -/
private theorem exists_range_eq [IsSimpleGroup S] : ∀ (m : ℕ) (D : Subgroup (Fin m → S)),
    (∀ i, D.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i) = ⊥ ∨
      D.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i) = ⊤) →
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (ρ : (Fin r → S) →* (Fin m → S)), ρ.range = D
  | 0, D, _ => ⟨0, 1, by
      ext x
      rw [Subsingleton.elim x 1]
      simp [D.one_mem]⟩
  | m + 1, D, hD => by
    set D' := D.map (tailHom m) with hD'def
    have hD' : ∀ i, D'.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i) = ⊥ ∨
        D'.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i) = ⊤ := by
      intro i
      rw [hD'def, Subgroup.map_map]
      exact hD i.succ
    obtain ⟨r', ρ', hρ'⟩ := exists_range_eq m D' hD'
    have hcons_tail : ∀ d : Fin (m + 1) → S,
        consOneHom m (tailHom m d) = Pi.mulSingle 0 (d 0)⁻¹ * d := by
      intro d
      ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun j => ?_) j
      · simp
      · simp
    rcases hD 0 with h0 | h0
    · -- every element of `D` is trivial in the first coordinate
      have hd0 : ∀ d ∈ D, d 0 = 1 := fun d hd => by
        have : d 0 ∈ D.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) 0) := ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
        rwa [h0, Subgroup.mem_bot] at this
      refine ⟨r', (consOneHom m).comp ρ', ?_⟩
      rw [MonoidHom.range_comp, hρ', hD'def, Subgroup.map_map]
      have hfix : ∀ d ∈ D, (consOneHom m).comp (tailHom m) d = d := fun d hd => by
        rw [MonoidHom.comp_apply, hcons_tail, hd0 d hd, inv_one, Pi.mulSingle_one, one_mul]
      ext x
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
        rw [hfix d hd]; exact hd
      · intro hx
        exact ⟨x, hx, hfix x hx⟩
    · let N := D.comap (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) (0 : Fin (m + 1)))
      have hN : N.Normal := ⟨fun n hn s => by
        obtain ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩ : s ∈ D.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) 0) :=
          h0 ▸ Subgroup.mem_top s
        have hconj : Pi.mulSingle (0 : Fin (m + 1)) (d 0 * n * (d 0)⁻¹) =
            d * Pi.mulSingle 0 n * d⁻¹ := by
          ext j
          by_cases hj : j = 0
          · subst hj; simp
          · simp [Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne hj]
        change Pi.mulSingle (0 : Fin (m + 1)) (d 0 * n * (d 0)⁻¹) ∈ D
        rw [hconj]
        exact D.mul_mem (D.mul_mem hd hn) (D.inv_mem hd)⟩
      rcases IsSimpleGroup.eq_bot_or_eq_top_of_normal N with hN' | hN'
      · -- forgetting the first coordinate is injective on `D`
        let τ : D →* (Fin m → S) := (tailHom m).comp D.subtype
        have hτ : Function.Injective τ := by
          refine (injective_iff_map_eq_one τ).mpr fun d hd => ?_
          have hd' : (d : Fin (m + 1) → S) = Pi.mulSingle 0 ((d : Fin (m + 1) → S) 0) := by
            have := hcons_tail d
            rw [show tailHom m d = τ d from rfl, hd, map_one] at this
            rw [Pi.mulSingle_inv, eq_inv_mul_iff_mul_eq, mul_one] at this
            exact this.symm
          have hmem : (d : Fin (m + 1) → S) 0 ∈ N := by
            change Pi.mulSingle 0 _ ∈ D
            rw [← hd']; exact d.2
          rw [hN', Subgroup.mem_bot] at hmem
          apply Subtype.ext
          rw [hd', hmem, Pi.mulSingle_one]
          rfl
        have hτrange : τ.range = D' := by
          rw [MonoidHom.range_comp, Subgroup.range_subtype]
        let e : D ≃* τ.range := MonoidHom.ofInjective hτ
        let ρ₁ : (Fin r' → S) →* τ.range :=
          ρ'.codRestrict τ.range (fun t => hτrange ▸ hρ' ▸ ⟨t, rfl⟩)
        refine ⟨r', D.subtype.comp (e.symm.toMonoidHom.comp ρ₁), ?_⟩
        apply le_antisymm
        · rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
          exact (e.symm (ρ₁ t)).2
        · intro d hd
          obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : τ ⟨d, hd⟩ ∈ ρ'.range := hρ' ▸ hτrange ▸ ⟨⟨d, hd⟩, rfl⟩
          refine ⟨t, ?_⟩
          have hρ₁ : ρ₁ t = e ⟨d, hd⟩ := Subtype.ext ht
          simp only [MonoidHom.comp_apply, MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom, hρ₁,
            MulEquiv.symm_apply_apply, Subgroup.coe_subtype]
      · -- `D` contains the first factor
        have hsingle : ∀ s : S, Pi.mulSingle (0 : Fin (m + 1)) s ∈ D := fun s =>
          (hN' ▸ Subgroup.mem_top s : s ∈ N)
        refine ⟨r' + 1, consHom ρ', le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
        · rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
          obtain ⟨d, hd, hdt⟩ : ρ' (Fin.tail t) ∈ D' := hρ' ▸ ⟨Fin.tail t, rfl⟩
          have hsplit : consHom ρ' t =
              Pi.mulSingle 0 (t 0) * consOneHom m (ρ' (Fin.tail t)) := by
            ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun j => ?_) j
            · simp
            · simp
          rw [hsplit, ← hdt, hcons_tail]
          exact D.mul_mem (hsingle _) (D.mul_mem (hsingle _) hd)
        · intro d hd
          obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : tailHom m d ∈ ρ'.range := hρ' ▸ ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
          refine ⟨Fin.cons (d 0) t, ?_⟩
          ext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun j => ?_) j
          · simp
          · simp [ht]

/-! ### The subgroup generated by the images of `S` -/

variable {ι : Type}

/-- The subgroup of `S^ι` generated by the images of all homomorphisms `S → S^ι` landing in `H`. -/
private def core (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) : Subgroup (ι → S) :=
  ⨆ (c : S →* (ι → S)) (_ : c.range ≤ H), c.range

private theorem core_le (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) : core H ≤ H := iSup₂_le fun _ h => h

private theorem range_le_core (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) (c : S →* (ι → S)) (hc : c.range ≤ H) :
    c.range ≤ core H :=
  le_iSup₂ (f := fun (c : S →* (ι → S)) (_ : c.range ≤ H) => c.range) c hc

private theorem conj_mem_core (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) {h : ι → S} (hh : h ∈ H) {d : ι → S}
    (hd : d ∈ core H) : h * d * h⁻¹ ∈ core H := by
  have : core H ≤ (core H).comap (MulAut.conj h).toMonoidHom := by
    refine iSup₂_le fun c hc => ?_
    rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
    refine range_le_core H ((MulAut.conj h).toMonoidHom.comp c) ?_ ⟨s, rfl⟩
    rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    exact H.mul_mem (H.mul_mem hh (hc ⟨t, rfl⟩)) (H.inv_mem hh)
  exact this hd

private theorem map_eval_core [IsSimpleGroup S] [Finite S] (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) (i : ι) :
    (core H).map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i) = ⊥ ∨
      (core H).map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i) = ⊤ := by
  by_cases h : ∃ c : S →* (ι → S), c.range ≤ H ∧
      ((Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i).comp c).range = ⊤
  · right
    obtain ⟨c, hc, htop⟩ := h
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← htop, ← MonoidHom.map_range]
    exact Subgroup.map_mono (range_le_core H c hc)
  · left
    rw [eq_bot_iff, Subgroup.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    refine iSup₂_le fun c hc => ?_
    rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
    rw [Subgroup.mem_comap, Subgroup.mem_bot]
    rcases eq_one_or_injective ((Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) i).comp c) with h1 | h1
    · exact DFunLike.congr_fun h1 s
    · exact absurd ⟨c, hc, MonoidHom.range_eq_top.mpr (Finite.injective_iff_surjective.mp h1)⟩ h

/-- If the image of a homomorphism `f` from a power of `S` lies in `ψ(H)`, then it lies in the
image under `ψ` of the subgroup generated by the images of `S` in `H`: each factor of the power is
an image of `S`, which lifts to `H` by `exists_lift`. -/
private theorem range_le_map_core [IsSimpleGroup S] [Finite S] [Finite ι] {A : Type} [Group A]
    (ψ : (ι → S) →* A) (H : Subgroup (ι → S)) {p : ℕ} (f : (Fin p → S) →* A)
    (hf : f.range ≤ H.map ψ) : f.range ≤ (core H).map ψ := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ (j : Fin p) (s : S), f (Pi.mulSingle j s) ∈ (core H).map ψ := by
    intro j s
    obtain ⟨c', hc'H, hc'⟩ := exists_lift ψ H (f.comp (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) j))
      (by rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩; exact hf ⟨_, rfl⟩)
    exact ⟨c' s, range_le_core H c' hc'H ⟨s, rfl⟩, DFunLike.congr_fun hc' s⟩
  rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
  have htop : (⊤ : Subgroup (Fin p → S)) ≤ ((core H).map ψ).comap f := by
    rw [← Subgroup.pi_top Set.univ, Subgroup.pi_le_iff]
    rintro j _ ⟨s, -, rfl⟩
    exact key j s
  exact htop (Subgroup.mem_top t)

end Powers

/-! ### Groups that are locally images of powers of `S` -/

/-- A group `G` is locally an image of powers of `S` when every finite subset of `G` lies in the
image of a homomorphism from some finite direct power of `S`. -/
private def IsLocPowImage (S : Type) [Group S] (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∀ s : Set G, s.Finite → ∃ (r : ℕ) (ρ : (Fin r → S) →* G), s ⊆ Set.range ρ

private theorem IsLocPowImage.of_surjective {S G H : Type} [Group S] [Group G] [Group H]
    (φ : G →* H) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hG : IsLocPowImage S G) : IsLocPowImage S H := by
  intro s hs
  obtain ⟨r, ρ, hρ⟩ := hG (Function.surjInv hφ '' s) (hs.image _)
  refine ⟨r, φ.comp ρ, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hρ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨t, by simp [ht, Function.surjInv_eq hφ]⟩

/-- **Closure under subdirect products.** If `R ≤ A × B` projects onto both factors and `A`, `B`
are locally images of powers of a finite simple group `S` with trivial centre, then every finite
subset of `R` lies in the image of a homomorphism from a power of `S` into `R`. -/
private theorem exists_hom_of_subdirect {S : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S] [Finite S]
    (hS : Subgroup.center S = ⊥) {A B : Type} [Group A] [Group B] (hA : IsLocPowImage S A)
    (hB : IsLocPowImage S B) (R : Subgroup (A × B)) (hR₁ : ∀ a, ∃ x ∈ R, x.1 = a)
    (hR₂ : ∀ b, ∃ x ∈ R, x.2 = b) (X : Set (A × B)) (hX : X.Finite) (hXR : X ⊆ R) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (ρ : (Fin r → S) →* A × B), ρ.range ≤ R ∧ X ⊆ Set.range ρ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨p, f, hf⟩ := hA (Prod.fst '' X) (hX.image _)
  obtain ⟨q, g, hg⟩ := hB (Prod.snd '' X) (hX.image _)
  choose ℓA hℓAR hℓA using hR₁
  choose ℓB hℓBR hℓB using hR₂
  set Y : Set (A × B) := X ∪ ℓA '' Set.range f ∪ ℓB '' Set.range g with hYdef
  have hY : Y.Finite :=
    (hX.union ((Set.finite_range f).image _)).union ((Set.finite_range g).image _)
  have hYR : Y ⊆ R := by
    rintro y ((hy | ⟨u, -, rfl⟩) | ⟨v, -, rfl⟩)
    exacts [hXR hy, hℓAR u, hℓBR v]
  obtain ⟨p', f', hf'⟩ := hA (Prod.fst '' Y) (hY.image _)
  obtain ⟨q', g', hg'⟩ := hB (Prod.snd '' Y) (hY.image _)
  let F : (Fin (p' + q') → S) →* A × B :=
    (f'.comp (precomp (Fin.castAdd q'))).prod (g'.comp (precomp (Fin.natAdd p')))
  set H : Subgroup (Fin (p' + q') → S) := R.comap F with hHdef
  have hYF : ∀ y ∈ Y, ∃ w ∈ H, F w = y := by
    intro y hy
    obtain ⟨w₁, hw₁⟩ := hf' ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨w₂, hw₂⟩ := hg' ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    have hFw : F (Fin.append w₁ w₂) = y := by
      ext
      · simp only [F, MonoidHom.prod_apply, MonoidHom.comp_apply]
        convert hw₁ using 2
        ext j; simp
      · simp only [F, MonoidHom.prod_apply, MonoidHom.comp_apply]
        convert hw₂ using 2
        ext j; simp
    exact ⟨_, by rw [hHdef, Subgroup.mem_comap, hFw]; exact hYR hy, hFw⟩
  set D := core H with hDdef
  obtain ⟨r, ρ, hρ⟩ := exists_range_eq (p' + q') D (map_eval_core H)
  set Q := D.map F with hQdef
  have hQ : ∀ d ∈ D, F d ∈ Q := fun d hd => ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
  have hQL : Q ≤ H.map F := Subgroup.map_mono (core_le H)
  refine ⟨r, F.comp ρ, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [MonoidHom.range_comp, hρ]
    exact Subgroup.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr (core_le H)
  -- the images of `f` and `g` lie in the projections of `Q`
  have hfQ : ∀ t, f t ∈ Q.map (MonoidHom.fst A B) := by
    intro t
    rw [hQdef, Subgroup.map_map]
    refine range_le_map_core _ H f ?_ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨w, hwH, hw⟩ := hYF (ℓA (f t)) (Or.inl (Or.inr ⟨f t, ⟨t, rfl⟩, rfl⟩))
    exact ⟨w, hwH, by simp [hw, hℓA]⟩
  have hgQ : ∀ t, g t ∈ Q.map (MonoidHom.snd A B) := by
    intro t
    rw [hQdef, Subgroup.map_map]
    refine range_le_map_core _ H g ?_ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨w, hwH, hw⟩ := hYF (ℓB (g t)) (Or.inr ⟨g t, ⟨t, rfl⟩, rfl⟩)
    exact ⟨w, hwH, by simp [hw, hℓB]⟩
  -- `Q` is normalized by `F(H)`
  have hnorm : ∀ y ∈ H.map F, ∀ x ∈ Q, y * x * y⁻¹ ∈ Q := by
    rintro _ ⟨h, hh, rfl⟩ _ ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨h * d * h⁻¹, conj_mem_core H hh hd, by simp⟩
  have hFρ : ∀ t, F (ρ t) ∈ Q := fun t => hQ _ (hρ ▸ ⟨t, rfl⟩)
  intro x hx
  have hxQ : x ∈ Q := by
    obtain ⟨w, hwH, hw⟩ := hYF x (Or.inl (Or.inl hx))
    have hxL : x ∈ H.map F := ⟨w, hwH, hw⟩
    obtain ⟨t₁, ht₁⟩ := hf ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨t₂, ht₂⟩ := hg ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨q₀, hq₀, hq₀1⟩ := hfQ t₁
    obtain ⟨q₂, hq₂, hq₂2⟩ := hgQ t₂
    set y := q₀⁻¹ * x with hydef
    have hyL : y ∈ H.map F := (H.map F).mul_mem ((H.map F).inv_mem (hQL hq₀)) hxL
    have hy1 : y.1 = 1 := by
      simp only [MonoidHom.coe_fst] at hq₀1
      simp [hydef, hq₀1, ht₁]
    have hy2 : y.2 ∈ Q.map (MonoidHom.snd A B) := by
      refine ⟨q₀⁻¹ * q₂, Q.mul_mem (Q.inv_mem hq₀) hq₂, ?_⟩
      simp only [MonoidHom.coe_snd] at hq₂2
      simp [hydef, hq₂2, ht₂]
    let M : Subgroup B := Q.comap (MonoidHom.inr A B)
    let ρB : (Fin r → S) →* B := (MonoidHom.snd A B).comp (F.comp ρ)
    have hρB : ρB.range = Q.map (MonoidHom.snd A B) := by
      rw [MonoidHom.range_comp, MonoidHom.range_comp, hρ]
    have hy2M : y.2 ∈ M := by
      refine mem_of_forall_commutator_mem_range hS ρB M ?_ (hρB ▸ hy2) ?_
      · intro m hm t
        have h1 : F (ρ t) * (MonoidHom.inr A B m) * (F (ρ t))⁻¹ ∈ Q :=
          Q.mul_mem (Q.mul_mem (hFρ t) hm) (Q.inv_mem (hFρ t))
        have h2 : F (ρ t) * (MonoidHom.inr A B m) * (F (ρ t))⁻¹ =
            MonoidHom.inr A B (ρB t * m * (ρB t)⁻¹) := by
          ext <;> simp [ρB]
        rw [h2] at h1
        exact h1
      · intro t
        have h1 : y * F (ρ t) * y⁻¹ * (F (ρ t))⁻¹ ∈ Q :=
          Q.mul_mem (hnorm y hyL _ (hFρ t)) (Q.inv_mem (hFρ t))
        have h2 : y * F (ρ t) * y⁻¹ * (F (ρ t))⁻¹ =
            MonoidHom.inr A B (y.2 * ρB t * y.2⁻¹ * (ρB t)⁻¹) := by
          ext
          · simp [hy1]
          · simp [ρB]
        rw [h2] at h1
        exact h1
    have hyQ : y ∈ Q := by
      have : y = MonoidHom.inr A B y.2 := Prod.ext hy1 rfl
      rw [this]; exact hy2M
    have : x = q₀ * y := by simp [hydef]
    rw [this]; exact Q.mul_mem hq₀ hyQ
  obtain ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩ := hxQ
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ : d ∈ ρ.range := hρ ▸ hd
  exact ⟨t, rfl⟩

/-- `S` itself is locally an image of powers of `S`. -/
private theorem isLocPowImage_self (S : Type) [Group S] : IsLocPowImage S S := fun _ _ =>
  ⟨1, Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ => S) 0, fun x _ => ⟨fun _ => x, rfl⟩⟩

/-- The groups that are locally images of powers of `S` form a formation. -/
private theorem isFormation_isLocPowImage {S : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S] [Finite S]
    (hS : Subgroup.center S = ⊥) : IsFormation (fun G _ => IsLocPowImage S G) := by
  refine ⟨⟨S, inferInstance, isLocPowImage_self S⟩,
    fun G H _ _ φ hφ hG => hG.of_surjective φ hφ, ?_⟩
  intro G _ N₁ N₂ _ _ h₁ h₂
  let p₁ : G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂) →* G ⧸ N₁ :=
    QuotientGroup.map _ _ (MonoidHom.id G) (by simp)
  let p₂ : G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂) →* G ⧸ N₂ :=
    QuotientGroup.map _ _ (MonoidHom.id G) (by simp)
  let e := p₁.prod p₂
  have he : Function.Injective e := by
    refine (injective_iff_map_eq_one e).mpr fun k hk => ?_
    induction k using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
    | H g =>
      simp only [e, p₁, p₂, MonoidHom.prod_apply, Prod.mk_eq_one, QuotientGroup.map_mk,
        MonoidHom.id_apply, QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff] at hk
      exact (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff g).mpr ⟨hk.1, hk.2⟩
  have hR : IsLocPowImage S e.range := by
    intro s hs
    obtain ⟨r, ρ, hρR, hρ⟩ := exists_hom_of_subdirect hS h₁ h₂ e.range
      (fun a => by
        induction a using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
        | H g => exact ⟨e (g : G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂)), ⟨_, rfl⟩, rfl⟩)
      (fun b => by
        induction b using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
        | H g => exact ⟨e (g : G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂)), ⟨_, rfl⟩, rfl⟩)
      (Subtype.val '' s) (hs.image _) (by rintro _ ⟨x, -, rfl⟩; exact x.2)
    refine ⟨r, ρ.codRestrict e.range fun t => hρR ⟨t, rfl⟩, fun x hx => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hρ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨t, Subtype.ext ht⟩
  exact hR.of_surjective (MonoidHom.ofInjective he).symm.toMonoidHom
    (MonoidHom.ofInjective he).symm.surjective

/-! ### The axioms -/

/-- The power `S^(Sᵏ)` of `S`, whose elements index the variables of the `k`-th axiom. -/
private abbrev Idx (S : Type) (k : ℕ) : Type := (Fin k → S) → S

/-- The product of two terms of the language of groups. -/
private noncomputable def mulTerm {α : Type} (t₁ t₂ : groupLanguage.Term α) :
    groupLanguage.Term α :=
  Term.func (GroupFunction.mul : groupLanguage.Functions 2) ![t₁, t₂]

private theorem realize_mulTerm {α : Type} (G : Type) [Group G] (v : α → G)
    (t₁ t₂ : groupLanguage.Term α) :
    @Term.realize groupLanguage G (groupLanguageStructure G) α v (mulTerm t₁ t₂) =
      @Term.realize groupLanguage G (groupLanguageStructure G) α v t₁ *
        @Term.realize groupLanguage G (groupLanguageStructure G) α v t₂ := rfl

/-- The `k`-th axiom: for all `x₀, …, x_{k-1}` there are elements `y_u`, one for each `u` in
`S^(Sᵏ)`, with `y_{uv} = y_u y_v` for all `u, v`, such that each `xᵢ` is one of the `y_u`. -/
private noncomputable def powSentence (S : Type) [Group S] [Finite S] (k : ℕ) :
    groupLanguage.Sentence :=
  Formula.iAlls (Fin k) <|
    Formula.iExs (Idx S k) <|
      (Formula.iInf fun (p : Idx S k × Idx S k) =>
        Term.equal (var (Sum.inr (p.1 * p.2)))
          (mulTerm (var (Sum.inr p.1)) (var (Sum.inr p.2)))) ⊓
      (Formula.iInf fun (i : Fin k) => Formula.iSup fun (u : Idx S k) =>
        Term.equal (var (Sum.inl (Sum.inr i))) (var (Sum.inr u)))

private theorem realize_powSentence {S : Type} [Group S] [Finite S] (G : Type) [Group G]
    (k : ℕ) :
    @Sentence.Realize groupLanguage G (groupLanguageStructure G) (powSentence S k) ↔
      ∀ x : Fin k → G, ∃ y : Idx S k → G,
        (∀ p : Idx S k × Idx S k, y (p.1 * p.2) = y p.1 * y p.2) ∧ ∀ i, ∃ u, x i = y u := by
  let _ := groupLanguageStructure G
  simp only [powSentence, Sentence.Realize, Formula.realize_iAlls, Formula.realize_iExs,
    Formula.realize_inf, Formula.realize_iInf, Formula.realize_iSup, Formula.realize_equal,
    realize_mulTerm, Term.realize_var, Sum.elim_inr, Sum.elim_inl]

private theorem isLocPowImage_iff_model {S : Type} [Group S] [Finite S] (G : Type) [Group G] :
    IsLocPowImage S G ↔
      @Theory.Model groupLanguage G (groupLanguageStructure G) (Set.range (powSentence S)) := by
  let _ := groupLanguageStructure G
  rw [Theory.model_iff, Set.forall_mem_range]
  simp only [realize_powSentence]
  constructor
  · intro hG k x
    obtain ⟨r, ρ, hρ⟩ := hG (Set.range x) (Set.finite_range x)
    choose t ht using fun i => hρ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨fun u => ρ (precomp (fun j i => t i j) u), fun p => by simp [map_mul],
      fun i => ⟨fun v => v i, ?_⟩⟩
    rw [← ht i]
    rfl
  · intro hT s hs
    obtain ⟨k, x, hx⟩ := hs.fin_embedding
    obtain ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩ := hT k x
    obtain ⟨n, ⟨e⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin (Fin k → S)
    let ρ₀ : Idx S k →* G := MonoidHom.mk' y fun a b => hy (a, b)
    refine ⟨n, ρ₀.comp (precomp ⇑e), ?_⟩
    rw [← hx]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hxy i
    refine ⟨u ∘ e.symm, ?_⟩
    have hpre : precomp ⇑e (u ∘ e.symm) = u := by
      ext v; simp
    rw [MonoidHom.comp_apply, hpre, hu]
    rfl

private theorem isAxiomatizable_isLocPowImage {S : Type} [Group S] [Finite S] :
    IsAxiomatizable (fun G _ => IsLocPowImage S G) :=
  ⟨Set.range (powSentence S), isLocPowImage_iff_model⟩

/-! ### Not a variety -/

/-- The class is not a variety: it contains `S`, but not the cyclic subgroup generated by a
nontrivial element of `S`. -/
private theorem not_isVariety_isLocPowImage {S : Type} [Group S] [IsSimpleGroup S] [Finite S]
    (hS : Subgroup.center S = ⊥) : ¬ IsVariety (fun G _ => IsLocPowImage S G) := by
  rintro ⟨W, hW⟩
  have hSmem : IsLocPowImage S S := isLocPowImage_self S
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_ne (1 : S)
  let T : Subgroup S := Subgroup.zpowers g
  have hTtop : T ≠ ⊤ := by
    intro hT
    have hgc : g ∈ Subgroup.center S := by
      rw [Subgroup.mem_center_iff]
      intro h
      obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Subgroup.mem_zpowers_iff.mp
        (show h ∈ T by rw [hT]; exact Subgroup.mem_top h)
      exact (Commute.zpow_left (Commute.refl g) n).eq
    rw [hS, Subgroup.mem_bot] at hgc
    exact hg hgc
  have hcard : Nat.card T < Nat.card S := by
    refine lt_of_le_of_ne (Subgroup.card_le_card_group T) fun h => hTtop ?_
    exact Subgroup.eq_top_of_le_card _ h.ge
  have hTnot : ¬ IsLocPowImage S T := by
    intro hT
    obtain ⟨r, ρ, hρ⟩ := hT {⟨g, Subgroup.mem_zpowers g⟩} (Set.finite_singleton _)
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hρ rfl
    have hρ1 : ∀ t, ρ t = 1 := by
      intro t
      rw [← MonoidHom.mem_ker]
      refine Subgroup.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem t fun i => ?_
      rcases eq_one_or_injective (ρ.comp (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S) i)) with h1 | h1
      · exact DFunLike.congr_fun h1 (t i)
      · exact absurd (Nat.card_le_card_of_injective _ h1) (not_le.mpr hcard)
    rw [hρ1] at ht
    exact hg (congrArg Subtype.val ht).symm
  -- a variety is closed under subgroups
  apply hTnot
  refine (hW T).mpr ?_
  intro w hw x
  have h := (hW S).mp hSmem w hw (T.subtype ∘ x)
  have hlift : T.subtype (FreeGroup.lift x w) = FreeGroup.lift (T.subtype ∘ x) w :=
    FreeGroup.lift_unique (T.subtype.comp (FreeGroup.lift x)) fun a => by simp
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [← Subgroup.coe_subtype, hlift, h, map_one]

/--
**Not every axiomatizable formation of groups is a variety.** The Gaglione–Spellman question
(Kourovka 14.32) has a negative answer: it is not the case that every first-order axiomatizable
formation of groups is a variety, that is, some class of groups is a formation and is first-order
axiomatizable but is not a variety.

Kearnes proved more: every variety of groups that contains a finite non-solvable group contains a
first-order axiomatizable subformation that is not a variety.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory:
The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem
14.32 (A. M. Gaglione, D. Spellman); resolution: K. A. Kearnes, J. Group Theory 13 (2010), no. 2,
233-241, Kourovka Archive, Problem 14.32: every variety of groups containing a finite non-solvable
member contains an axiomatic subformation that is not a variety (answer: No).
-/
theorem axiomatizableFormationIsVariety_refuted : ¬ axiomatizableFormationIsVariety := by
  intro h
  have : IsSimpleGroup (alternatingGroup (Fin 5)) := alternatingGroup.isSimpleGroup (by simp)
  have hS : Subgroup.center (alternatingGroup (Fin 5)) = ⊥ :=
    alternatingGroup.center_eq_bot (by simp)
  exact not_isVariety_isLocPowImage hS
    (h _ (isFormation_isLocPowImage hS) isAxiomatizable_isLocPowImage)

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AxiomatizableFormationVarietyKourovka14Problem32Wanted
